    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d964">

                <pb facs="0947" n="781" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg781"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 714.1515/28</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Ewing to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-16T11:00:00-05:48">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 16, 1917, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s November 12, 5 p.m. Government replies accepting offer United States
                    to mediate boundary dispute with Guatemala. This request for mediation
                    originally suggested by Honduras to United States March 5 last. Honduras denies
                    presence of troops numbering neighborhood thousand, ordinarily maintaining only
                    twenty-nine soldiers this district with additional twenty at present.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ewing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
